# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — agent instructions

This project uses s3lab-ai-kit standards (git submodule at `.ai-kit/`).

## Read these first

Before making any change, read in order:

1. `.ai-kit/ai/core.md` — main context, stack, workflow, all conventions
2. `.ai/project-context.md` — this project's specific context and deviations

## Available workflows

Read `.ai-kit/ai/commands/` for pipelines:

- `.ai-kit/ai/commands/feature.md` — implement a feature end-to-end
- `.ai-kit/ai/commands/bugfix.md` — diagnose and fix a bug
- `.ai-kit/ai/commands/review-pr.md` — review an existing PR
- `.ai-kit/ai/commands/sync-contract.md` — sync OpenAPI between back and front

## Specialized agent prompts

If delegating to a specialist persona, read its prompt first from `.ai-kit/ai/agents/`:

- `orchestrator` — decompose tasks
- `backend-dotnet` — .NET 10 implementation
- `frontend-angular` — Angular implementation
- `api-contract` — OpenAPI sync
- `devops` — Docker, compose, CI
- `tester` — generate and run tests
- `reviewer` — pre-merge review
- `designer` — UX specs and mockups

## Project overrides

If `.ai/overrides/<name>.md` exists, it takes precedence over the kit default
for that agent or convention.
